# Copy to `web/.env.local` for web values that are yours rather than the project's. Gitignored;
# this example is not.
#
#   cp web/.env.local.example web/.env.local
#
# This is the most specific file the web app reads, so anything set here wins over everything but
# a real environment variable. Use it only for something that must not follow the repo-wide
# value — otherwise put it in `../.env.local`, which carries the full precedence order.
#
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables are readable from browser code, and vite exposes every one it
# finds, so never put a secret in a web env file at all: it would ship inside the bundle.

# Point the dev server at an api running somewhere other than the committed default — another
# port, a container, or a colleague's machine. Development only: a build talks to whatever origin
# serves it. Must match the api's PORT.
#VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:3000
